@page "/counter-signals"
@rendermode InteractiveServer

<PageTitle>Counter (Signals)</PageTitle>

<h1>Counter (Signals)</h1>

<p>Trace of the <em>counter-signals</em> variant of <code>HtmlFlow-Datastar-Examples</code>.
    In BRHC a <code>count</code> signal lives in the client and is synchronised over SSE
    (<code>data-init @@get('/counter/events')</code>); the button issues <code>@@post</code> and the server
    emits the new value on the stream. Here the value is a C# field in the circuit: the
"synchronisation" is SignalR itself. <strong>Teaching note:</strong> the counter/counter-signals distinction collapses
    in Blazor - there is no separate typed signal for the UHF to type.</p>

    <div class="demo-box">
        <p class="fs-3">Current count: <strong>@count</strong></p>
        <button class="btn btn-primary" @onclick="Increment">Increment</button>
        <button class="btn btn-secondary" @onclick="Decrement">Decrement</button>
    </div>

@code {
    // Estado no servidor (circuito Blazor), cf. MutableStateFlow<Int> do Ktor.
    private int count = 0;

    private void Increment() => count++;
    private void Decrement() => count--;
}